@SecureToolKitAPI_HostAddress = http://localhost:5149

### Health

GET {{SecureToolKitAPI_HostAddress}}/health

### Discover the supported methods

GET {{SecureToolKitAPI_HostAddress}}/api/keygen/methods
Accept: application/json

###

GET {{SecureToolKitAPI_HostAddress}}/api/encrypt/methods
Accept: application/json

###

GET {{SecureToolKitAPI_HostAddress}}/api/signature/methods
Accept: application/json

### AES-GCM round trip: generate key, encrypt, decrypt.
# The keys below are generated locally for manual testing only. Never paste a real key here.

# @name generateAesKey
GET {{SecureToolKitAPI_HostAddress}}/api/keygen/aes?keySize=256
Accept: application/json

###

# @name encryptWithAes
POST {{SecureToolKitAPI_HostAddress}}/api/encrypt/aes-gcm
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "key": "{{generateAesKey.response.body.$.key}}",
  "message": "Hello World"
}

###

POST {{SecureToolKitAPI_HostAddress}}/api/decrypt/aes-gcm
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "key": "{{generateAesKey.response.body.$.key}}",
  "encryptedMessage": "{{encryptWithAes.response.body.$.encryptedMessage}}"
}

### RSA-OAEP round trip: encrypt with the public key, decrypt with the private key.

# @name generateRsaKeys
GET {{SecureToolKitAPI_HostAddress}}/api/keygen/rsa?keySize=2048
Accept: application/json

###

# @name encryptWithRsa
POST {{SecureToolKitAPI_HostAddress}}/api/encrypt/rsa-oaep
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "key": "{{generateRsaKeys.response.body.$.publicKey}}",
  "message": "Hello World"
}

###

POST {{SecureToolKitAPI_HostAddress}}/api/decrypt/rsa-oaep
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "key": "{{generateRsaKeys.response.body.$.privateKey}}",
  "encryptedMessage": "{{encryptWithRsa.response.body.$.encryptedMessage}}"
}

### ECDH + AES-GCM hybrid round trip: encrypt with the recipient public key, decrypt with the private key.

# @name generateEccHillmanKeys
GET {{SecureToolKitAPI_HostAddress}}/api/keygen/EccHillman?keySize=256
Accept: application/json

###

# @name encryptWithEccHillman
POST {{SecureToolKitAPI_HostAddress}}/api/encrypt/ecc-hillman
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "key": "{{generateEccHillmanKeys.response.body.$.publicKey}}",
  "message": "Hello World"
}

###

POST {{SecureToolKitAPI_HostAddress}}/api/decrypt/ecc-hillman
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "key": "{{generateEccHillmanKeys.response.body.$.privateKey}}",
  "encryptedMessage": "{{encryptWithEccHillman.response.body.$.encryptedMessage}}"
}

### ECDSA sign and verify: sign with the private key, verify with the public key.

# @name generateEccDssKeys
GET {{SecureToolKitAPI_HostAddress}}/api/keygen/EccDss?keySize=256
Accept: application/json

###

# @name signWithEccDss
POST {{SecureToolKitAPI_HostAddress}}/api/signature/ecc-dss/sign
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "key": "{{generateEccDssKeys.response.body.$.privateKey}}",
  "message": "Hello World"
}

###

POST {{SecureToolKitAPI_HostAddress}}/api/signature/ecc-dss/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "key": "{{generateEccDssKeys.response.body.$.publicKey}}",
  "message": "Hello World",
  "signature": "{{signWithEccDss.response.body.$.signature}}"
}

### HMAC-SHA256 sign and verify: the same secret is used for both.

# @name generateHmacSecret
GET {{SecureToolKitAPI_HostAddress}}/api/keygen/hmac?keySize=256
Accept: application/json

###

# @name signWithHmac
POST {{SecureToolKitAPI_HostAddress}}/api/signature/hmac-sha256/sign
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "key": "{{generateHmacSecret.response.body.$.key}}",
  "message": "Hello World"
}

###

POST {{SecureToolKitAPI_HostAddress}}/api/signature/hmac-sha256/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "key": "{{generateHmacSecret.response.body.$.key}}",
  "message": "Hello World",
  "signature": "{{signWithHmac.response.body.$.signature}}"
}

### Method-agnostic key generation

POST {{SecureToolKitAPI_HostAddress}}/api/keygen/random
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "keySize": 512
}

### Rejected requests: expect 400 with a problem response and no cryptographic detail

GET {{SecureToolKitAPI_HostAddress}}/api/keygen/aes?keySize=100
Accept: application/json

###

POST {{SecureToolKitAPI_HostAddress}}/api/encrypt/not-a-method
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "key": "{{generateAesKey.response.body.$.key}}",
  "message": "Hello World"
}

###

POST {{SecureToolKitAPI_HostAddress}}/api/decrypt/aes-gcm
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "key": "{{generateAesKey.response.body.$.key}}",
  "encryptedMessage": "not-base64!!"
}

###
